  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The current best (config_016: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.6776 accuracy at only 5.90 GPU hours. The two most promising untested axes are upgrading the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) and upgrading aggregation (avgpool → transformer). I choose config_010 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) as a clean single-variable extension of the current best: it replaces only the image encoder with a much stronger ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet while preserving the proven scvi_n200 RNA encoder and weighted fusion. This isolates the image-encoder contribution and tells us whether the bottleneck is image representation quality. If it helps, the next step is clearly to add transformer aggregation (config_020); if it doesn't, we pivot to aggregation. Expected cost is moderate (~15–25 GPU hours) due to ViT-L's larger parameter count, but well below config_003's 36.42 hours, leaving ample budget for follow-ups."
}

